Purpose
The floating snatch deadlift on riser increases the strengthening of the pull from the floor and the postural strength of the first pull. The riser ensures full range of motion in the floating position, i.e. the lifter can reach the actual starting position (or deeper) in the bottom rather than stopping short as happens in a floating lift from the floor.
